.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PurposeOS
is a Linux desktop automation daemon designed for personal productivity workflows.
It provides scheduled reminders, scheduled desktop actions, quick note capture,
a full PySide6 graphical dashboard, terminal management commands, and basic
focus/statistics tracking.

PurposeOS is built around three main interfaces:

.TP
.B Daemon
The background daemon is started by
.BR purposeos-daemon .
It loads the YAML configuration file, initializes logging, starts the application
tracker, builds scheduled reminder and action jobs, watches the configuration
file for changes, and handles shutdown/reload signals.

.TP
.B CLI
The
.B adctl
command is the primary administration interface. It controls the daemon,
manages reminders, manages scheduled actions, opens the GUI, manages notes,
prints statistics, and performs package self-management tasks.

.TP
.B GUI
The graphical interface is implemented with PySide6 and can be launched with
.BR "adctl gui" .
It provides sections for reminders, actions, notes, statistics, and settings.
A lightweight floating quick-note window can be launched with
.BR "adctl quicknote" .

PurposeOS is installed as a per-user desktop service, not as a system-wide root
daemon. The service runs through
.BR systemd --user ,
starts after the graphical session is available, imports desktop session
environment variables, and restarts automatically on failure.

The daemon uses a YAML configuration file for persistent reminders, actions,
and settings. It automatically creates a skeleton configuration file if none
exists. Configuration changes can be live-reloaded through
.B adctl reload
or by saving the configuration file while the watcher is active.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS Daemon control commands
.TP
.B adctl start
Start the PurposeOS daemon. The command first attempts to start the user
systemd service
.BR purposeos.service .
If systemd startup fails, it falls back to launching the Python daemon module
directly.

.TP
.B adctl stop
Stop the running daemon by sending
.B SIGTERM
to the process ID recorded in the daemon PID file.

.TP
.B adctl restart
Stop the daemon, wait briefly, and start it again.

.TP
.B adctl reload
Live-reload the daemon configuration by sending
.B SIGHUP
to the running daemon process.

.TP
.B adctl status
Show whether the daemon is running and display its process ID when available.

.TP
.B adctl logs
Show recent daemon log lines from the PurposeOS log file.

.TP
.BI "adctl logs \-n " LINES
Show the last
.I LINES
lines from the daemon log. The default is 50 lines.

.TP
.B adctl enable
Enable
.B purposeos.service
to start automatically at user login.

.TP
.B adctl disable
Disable automatic startup of
.B purposeos.service
at user login.

.SS GUI commands
.TP
.B adctl gui
Open the full PurposeOS graphical dashboard.

.TP
.B adctl gui --notes
Open the graphical dashboard directly on the Notes tab.

.TP
.B adctl quicknote
Open the floating quick-note window.

.SS Reminder commands
.TP
.B adctl reminders list
List configured reminders with their number, title, trigger, urgency, and
enabled state.

.TP
.BI "adctl reminders add --message " TEXT
Add a reminder. If no trigger option is provided, the reminder uses the
.B boot
trigger.

.TP
.BI "adctl reminders add --message " TEXT " --at " HH:MM
Add a daily reminder at the specified time.

.TP
.BI "adctl reminders add --message " TEXT " --every " MINUTES
Add an interval reminder that repeats every
.I MINUTES
minutes.

.TP
.BI "adctl reminders add --message " TEXT " --day " DAY
Add a weekly reminder. The
.I DAY
argument may be a weekday such as
.BR mon ,
.BR tue ,
.BR wed ,
.BR thu ,
.BR fri ,
.BR sat ,
or
.BR sun .

.TP
.BI "--title " NAME
Set the reminder title. The default title is
.BR Reminder .

.TP
.BR "--urgency " "low|normal|critical"
Set the notification urgency. The default is
.BR normal .

.TP
.BI "--sound " SOUND
Set a sound name or sound file path for the reminder.

.TP
.B --no-overlay
Use a standard desktop notification instead of the screen-wide overlay.

.TP
.BI "--close " SECONDS
Set the auto-close time for non-critical screen-wide overlays. The default is
30 seconds.

.TP
.BI "adctl reminders remove " NUMBER
Remove the reminder identified by
.I NUMBER
from
.BR "adctl reminders list" .

.TP
.BI "adctl reminders enable " NUMBER
Enable the reminder identified by
.IR NUMBER .

.TP
.BI "adctl reminders disable " NUMBER
Disable the reminder identified by
.I NUMBER
without deleting it.

.SS Action commands
.TP
.B adctl actions list
List configured scheduled actions with their number, type, target, trigger,
and enabled state.

.TP
.BI "adctl actions add --type " TYPE " --target " TARGET
Add a scheduled action. If no trigger option is provided, the action uses the
.B boot
trigger.

.TP
.BR "--type " "open_file|open_app|run_command|open_url|show_notification"
Set the action type.

.TP
.BI "--target " TARGET
Set the action target. The meaning depends on the action type:
a file path for
.BR open_file ,
an application command for
.BR open_app ,
a shell command for
.BR run_command ,
a URL for
.BR open_url ,
or notification data for
.BR show_notification .

.TP
.BI "--at " HH:MM
Run the action daily at the specified time.

.TP
.BI "--every " MINUTES
Run the action repeatedly every
.I MINUTES
minutes.

.TP
.BI "--day " DAY
Run the action weekly on the specified day.

.TP
.BI "adctl actions remove " NUMBER
Remove the action identified by
.I NUMBER
from
.BR "adctl actions list" .

.TP
.BI "adctl actions enable " NUMBER
Enable the action identified by
.IR NUMBER .

.TP
.BI "adctl actions disable " NUMBER
Disable the action identified by
.I NUMBER
without deleting it.

.SS Notes commands
.TP
.B adctl notes list
List saved notes.

.TP
.B adctl notes new
Create a new note using the terminal editor.

.TP
.BI "adctl notes show " NUMBER
Print the selected note to standard output.

.TP
.BI "adctl notes edit " NUMBER
Edit the selected note in the terminal editor.

.TP
.BI "adctl notes delete " NUMBER
Delete the selected note.

.SS Statistics commands
.TP
.B adctl stats
Show today's statistics. This defaults to the same behavior as
.BR "adctl stats today" .

.TP
.B adctl stats today
Show today's tracked application usage statistics.

.TP
.B adctl stats week
Show this week's tracked application usage statistics.

.TP
.B adctl stats notifications
Show notification interaction statistics.

.TP
.BI "adctl stats range " START " " END
Show tracked statistics for a date range. Dates must use
.B YYYY-MM-DD
format.

.TP
.BI "adctl stats app " APP_NAME
Show a per-application daily breakdown for the specified application.

.TP
.BI "adctl stats app " APP_NAME " --days " DAYS
Show a per-application breakdown for the last
.I DAYS
days. The default is 7 days.

.TP
.B adctl stats diagnose
Run diagnostics for the statistics tracker. This checks the SQLite database,
graphical session environment variables, and active-window detection methods.

.SS Package management commands
.TP
.B adctl update
Run the recorded project update script from the source path saved during
installation.

.TP
.B adctl uninstall
Run the installed uninstaller from the PurposeOS manifest directory.

.TP
.B adctl version
Print the installed PurposeOS version.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/automation-daemon/config.yaml
Main PurposeOS YAML configuration file. Contains global settings, reminders,
and actions.

.TP
.I ~/.config/automation-daemon/notes/
Default directory for plain text notes.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/automation-daemon/tracker.db
SQLite database used for application tracking and notification interaction
statistics.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/automation-daemon/logs/daemon.log
Main daemon log file.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/automation-daemon/daemon.pid
PID file written by the daemon while it is running.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/automation-daemon/scheduler_state.yaml
Scheduler state file used to preserve interval scheduling information and boot
detection state.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/purposeos/uninstall.sh
Installed uninstaller script used by
.BR "adctl uninstall" .

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/purposeos/source_path
Recorded source tree path used by
.BR "adctl update" .

.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/purposeos.service
User-level systemd service unit for the PurposeOS daemon.

.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/adctl
User command wrapper for the PurposeOS CLI.

.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/purposeos-daemon
User command wrapper for the daemon entry point.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/purposeos-gui.desktop
Desktop launcher for the full PurposeOS GUI.

.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications/purposeos-quicknote.desktop
Desktop launcher for the quick-note window.

.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is written in YAML. PurposeOS ignores unknown YAML keys
to preserve forward compatibility with older configuration files.

A minimal configuration example:

.EX
settings:
  log_level: INFO
  sound_command: paplay
  notification_timeout_ms: 30000
  screen_wide_default: true
  tracker_poll_interval_sec: 5
  notes_dir: ""
  language: en

reminders:
  - title: "Morning Check-in"
    message: "Review your task list."
    trigger: daily
    trigger_value: "09:00"
    urgency: normal
    screen_wide: true
    auto_close_sec: 30
    enabled: true

actions:
  - action_type: open_file
    trigger: boot
    target: ~/Documents/todo.txt
    enabled: true
.EE

Supported reminder triggers and action triggers are:

.TP
.B boot
Run shortly after daemon startup when a new system boot is detected.

.TP
.B daily
Run every day at a time specified by
.BR trigger_value ,
usually in
.B HH:MM
format.

.TP
.B interval_minutes
Run repeatedly every
.B trigger_value
minutes.

.TP
.B weekly
Run weekly on the weekday specified by
.BR trigger_value .

.SH ENVIRONMENT
PurposeOS normally runs as a user systemd service inside a graphical desktop
session. The service imports or passes the following environment variables when
available:

.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display identifier.

.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland display identifier.

.TP
.B DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS
D-Bus session bus address, required by many desktop integration components.

.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Runtime directory used by desktop session services.

.TP
.B XAUTHORITY
X11 authority file path.

.TP
.B HOME
User home directory.

.TP
.B USER
Current user name.

.TP
.B PYTHONUNBUFFERED
The service sets this to
.B 1
so daemon output is not buffered.

.SH EXAMPLES
Start the daemon:

.EX
adctl start
.EE

Check daemon status:

.EX
adctl status
.EE

Show the last 100 log lines:

.EX
adctl logs -n 100
.EE

Add a daily reminder:

.EX
adctl reminders add --message "Stand up" --at 11:00
.EE

Add an interval reminder:

.EX
adctl reminders add --message "Drink water" --every 60 --urgency low
.EE

Add an action that opens a file every morning:

.EX
adctl actions add --type open_file --target ~/todo.txt --at 09:00
.EE

Open the GUI:

.EX
adctl gui
.EE

Open the quick-note window:

.EX
adctl quicknote
.EE

View weekly statistics:

.EX
adctl stats week
.EE

Reload configuration without restarting:

.EX
adctl reload
.EE

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
If the daemon does not start, inspect the user service:

.EX
systemctl --user status purposeos.service
.EE

Inspect daemon logs:

.EX
adctl logs -n 100
.EE

Inspect journal logs:

.EX
journalctl --user -u purposeos.service
.EE

Reload the user systemd manager after editing the service file:

.EX
systemctl --user daemon-reload
.EE

Run statistics diagnostics:

.EX
adctl stats diagnose
.EE

